"$\\phi = 0$, $z = 0$","input":"The pulse of Piran, Safier, and Katz, of width $a$ and strength $\\alpha$: $e^{2\\psi} = \\left(\\alpha^2(1 - \\lambda_u\\lambda_v)^2 + (\\lambda_u + \\lambda_v)^2\\right)/\\left(\\alpha^2\\Xi^2 + (\\lambda_u - \\lambda_v)^2\\right)$, $e^{2\\gamma} = \\left(\\alpha^2(1 - \\lambda_u\\lambda_v)^2 + (\\lambda_u + \\lambda_v)^2\\right)/\\left((1 + \\lambda_u^2)(1 + \\lambda_v^2)\\right)$, and $\\omega = 2\\beta(\\alpha + \\alpha\\beta)a - \\alpha\\beta\\,\\Xi(\\lambda_u + \\lambda_v)^2a/\\left(\\sqrt{\\lambda_u\\lambda_v}\\left(\\alpha^2(1 - \\lambda_u\\lambda_v)^2 + (\\lambda_u + \\lambda_v)^2\\right)\\right)$, with $\\beta = \\sqrt{\\alpha^2 - 1}/\\alpha$, $\\Xi = 1 + \\lambda_u\\lambda_v + 2\\beta\\sqrt{\\lambda_u\\lambda_v}$, $a\\lambda_u = \\sqrt{a^2 + u^2} - u$, and $a\\lambda_v = \\sqrt{a^2 + v^2} + v$, at $\\alpha = 2$, checked to solve this spacetime's own field equations.","caption":["A pulse of Piran, Safier, and Katz ($\\alpha = 2$) on the plane of $t$ and $\\rho$. Its metric there, $e^{2(\\gamma - \\psi)}(-c^2dt^2 + d\\rho^2)$ whatever $\\omega$ is, keeps the rays at 45° and in the plane.","The pulse is deepest on the axis at $t = 0$ ($\\psi = -1.32$) and leaves just inside $\\rho = |ct|$."],"source":{"fields":["coords","parameters","metric_components","inverse_metric_components","kretschmann","domains","einstein_tensor"],"version":"d26a0015bb4c9859"},"slices":[{"view":"pulse","surface":0,"label":"$ct = 0\\,a$","version":"b8f573c9f9b1e0fc","lines":[[[0.0,0.1],[1.0,0.1]]],"points":[],"fills":[],"place":{"at":[1.0,0.1],"anchor":"tr","dx":0,"dy":1.3}},{"view":"pulse","surface":1,"label":"$ct = 0.5\\,a$","version":"3a001cb6c5ea5c8c","lines":[[[0.0,0.15],[1.0,0.15]]],"points":[],"fills":[],"place":{"at":[1.0,0.15],"anchor":"br","dx":0,"dy":-1.3}},{"view":"pulse","surface":2,"label":"$ct = 1\\,a$","version":"914d9be6f89847bc","lines":[[[0.0,0.2],[1.0,0.2]]],"points":[],"fills":[],"place":{"at":[0.0,0.2],"anchor":"bl","dx":0,"dy":-1